# g95-fu-renderer-direct: the toast of a frame the relay refused. The relay answers an oversize frame of the core's leg with
# `frame-too-large`; mixdog-remote (access/runtime.rs, Inbound::FrameTooLarge) now calls RemoteEvents::relay_payload_refused(bytes, limit) and
# tells the named phone with a relayPayloadRejected event. The windows hear it as the app-feed notification below
# (renderer/core-direct/api-sessions.ts `subscribeRelayPayloadRefused` reads `ui/relayPayloadRefused`; desktop-toasts.tsx shows it).
# The new file native/core/crates/mixdog-app-protocol/src/v2/relay_payload.rs is part of this fragment (UiRelayPayloadRefusedParams).

[methods]
# none

[server_requests]
# none

[notifications]
In notifications.rs, add `use crate::v2::relay_payload::UiRelayPayloadRefusedParams;` beside the other v2 imports, and beside UiProviderModelsChanged (after it):

    /// Node's `relay-payload-refused` event: the relay refused an oversize frame of the core's leg; the windows show the size and the ceiling.
    UiRelayPayloadRefused => "ui/relayPayloadRefused" (UiRelayPayloadRefusedParams) @app,

In v2/mod.rs add `pub mod relay_payload;` (after `pub mod pc_access;`).

[inventory]
In inventory.rs, beside the "terminalRemoteOpen" row (InventoryList::Operations), add:

    (
        InventoryList::Operations,
        "relayPayloadRefused",
        Target::Notification("ui/relayPayloadRefused"),
    ),

[free_text]
# none (bytes and limit are numbers)
